window.docContents[60].resolve({"/Lecture-1___-Motivation-and-Propositional-Logic/Worked-Examples/#Formal-Software-Verification--Lecture-1___-Motivation-and-Propositional-Logic--Worked-Examples--Double-Negation-Elimination":{"contents":"This direction requires classical reasoning. Classical.byContradiction discharges the assumption ¬P after deriving ⊥ from it together with ¬¬P.\n\n   [¬P]  [¬¬P]\n  ──────────────  ¬E\n        ⊥\n    ──────────  RAA\n        P\n   ───────────────  →I\n     ¬¬P → P\n\n\nexample (P : Prop) : ¬¬P → P :=\n  fun h => Classical.byContradiction (fun hnP => h hnP)\n\n\nexample (P : Prop) : ¬¬P → P := by\n  intro h\n  apply Classical.byContradiction\n  intro hnP\n  exact h hnP\n\n\n","context":"Formal Software Verification\u0009Lecture 1: Motivation and Propositional Logic\u0009Worked Examples","header":"1.8.5. Double Negation Elimination","id":"/Lecture-1___-Motivation-and-Propositional-Logic/Worked-Examples/#Formal-Software-Verification--Lecture-1___-Motivation-and-Propositional-Logic--Worked-Examples--Double-Negation-Elimination"}});